MG_FINDINGS = "Madagascar (MG) — findings for egao1980/cl-stack-calendars#45 item 7.\n\nMechanism: there is no standing statutory list. The Code du travail (Loi 2003-044 art. 81 al. 3; from 2024 Loi 2024-014\nart. 115) delegates to a decree, and the Government issues one decree per year 'fixant la liste des jours fériés, chômés\net payés au titre de l'année N'. Each decree is exhaustive (any other day needs its own decree 'publié une semaine à\nl'avance') and enters into force on radio/TV broadcast (urgency clause, Ord. 62-041). Texts read: CNLEGIS PDFs\n(cnlegis.gov.mg/uploads/D2024-108-VF.pdf, D2025-005-VF.pdf, D2026-006-VF.pdf, D2025-415-VF.pdf) and the CNLEGIS texts mirrored\nby textes.lexxika.com (PDF scans marked www.cnlegis.gov.mg, with JO references) for 2001-2022.\n\nIssue item 7 verdict:\n- Ascension, Lundi de Pentecôte (and Pâques, Pentecôte Sundays) ARE on every list 2006-2026 -> the starter must add\n  Ascension (Easter+39) and Whit Monday (Easter+50); Easter Monday, 1 Jan, 8 Mar, 29 Mar, 1 May, 26 Jun, 15 Aug, 1 Nov,\n  25 Dec are all confirmed.\n- 'No Islamic holidays' is WRONG for recent years: Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha are on the lists since 2013 — 'uniquement\n  pour les musulmans' 2013, 2014, 2016-2018; general (no restriction) in 2015 (additif 2015-524) and from 2019 (Décret\n  2019-1065 dropped the restriction) through 2026 ('suivant le calendrier fixé par la Communauté musulmane', date\n  announced by MTEFOP communiqué). They were NOT holidays in 2006, 2007, 2009, 2011, 2012. So cl-stack's 'Aïd every year\n  from 1960' is wrong before 2013, and its tabular dates should be replaced by announced dates; python-holidays (no Eid\n  at all) is wrong from 2013/2019.\n- 8 March: 'fériée et chômée uniquement pour les femmes' in every list 2007-2026 (2006: no restriction).\n- 25 May (Africa Day) in the starter: NOT on any list 2006-2026 -> remove. (Only 22 May 1998 OAU day decree 98-374 exists.)\n- 11 December: on the lists 2011-2014 only (Décret 2010-990 + yearly lists); absent 2015-2026. python-holidays has it every\n  year from 2011 -> wrong from 2015. 14 October: 2013 only (2014 entry abrogated by Décret 2014-1571).\n- No Sunday-in-lieu rule; holidays on Sunday are simply lost (2026: 8 Mar, 29 Mar, 1 Nov).\n- Mother's Day / Father's Day (python-holidays) are not on any list.\n- 2026 additions: Taombaovao Malagasy and a journée nationale de la culture (dates set separately; not confirmed).\n\nOne-off days by decree (all primary, CNLEGIS): 2001-12-24, 2001-12-31; 2004-12-24, 2004-12-31; 2005-10-31; 2007-01-19\n(investiture), 2007-04-04 (referendum), 2007-06-25 and 2007-12-24 (jours ponts), 2007-08-09 (JIOI), 2007-12-12 (communal\nelections); 2010-12-11; 2011-06-03; 2012-06-25, 2012-11-02, 2012-12-31; 2013-10-25, 2013-12-20 (elections; earlier dates\n24 Jul/25 Sep superseded); 2014-10-14 cancelled; 2025-04-23 (Décret 2025-415). Election days under art. 2 of the lists:\n2015-07-31, 2019-05-27, 2019-11-27, 2024-05-29, 2024-12-11 (dates from electoral calendars, not read).\n\nYears: primary 2006, 2007, 2009, 2011-2020, 2022, 2024-2026 (yearly decree read; Eid dates for 2020, 2024-2026 are\nsecondary news reports of ministry communiqués). Secondary: 2001, 2004, 2005, 2010 (one-off decree only, base list\nassumed), 2023 (news only). Missing: 2000, 2002, 2003, 2008, 2021, 2027 (no decree located; 2027 decree not yet issued).\nNot found: any decree for the 2018 and 2023 presidential election days (likely exist; see MG_ADHOC).\nSources not reachable: gem-madagascar.com communiqués list (404); Japanese embassy holiday PDFs (stalled).\n"


